{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8209a29f-eaec-43e8-aa02-5ae3ba6fdb5f","step":{"id":"intro","script":"A derivative tells us the slope of a curve at one specific point.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"heading","region":"A1","content":"Derivative = slope at a point"},{"op":"axes","id":"axes","region":"right","x":{"min":-2,"max":2,"label":"x"},"y":{"min":0,"max":4,"label":"y"}}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8209a29f-eaec-43e8-aa02-5ae3ba6fdb5f","step":{"id":"curve","script":"Consider the parabola y equals x squared, and focus where x equals one.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"parabola","axes_id":"axes","expr":"x^2","domain":[-2,2]},{"op":"text","id":"pointlabel","anchor":{"el":"axes","side":"below","gap":0.06},"content":"focus point: x = 1"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"At x equals one, is the parabola rising or falling?","expected_gist":"rising"}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8209a29f-eaec-43e8-aa02-5ae3ba6fdb5f","step":{"id":"tangent","script":"A tangent line matches the curve's direction exactly at that point.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"tangentline","axes_id":"axes","expr":"2*x-1","domain":[-0.5,2]},{"op":"text","id":"tangentlabel","anchor":{"el":"pointlabel","side":"below","gap":0.05},"content":"tangent slope = 2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8209a29f-eaec-43e8-aa02-5ae3ba6fdb5f","step":{"id":"result","script":"Therefore, the derivative of x squared at x equals one is two.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"derivresult","region":"B2","latex":"\\frac{d}{dx}(x^2)\\bigg|_{x=1}=2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
